## Session Handoff

### Phase 1 — Device Benchmark ✓ Complete

**RK3588 big.LITTLE benchmark** (bead `ob-8ms.3`):

| Cluster | Cores | Best GiB/s | Key finding |
|---|---|---|---|
| A76 big (cpu4-7) | 4× @ 2.3 GHz | 5.6 (0.8B conv) | 6–16% of spec BW |
| A55 little (cpu0-3) | 4× @ 1.8 GHz | 1.2 (0.8B decay) | 4–5× slower than big despite 1.28× clock ratio |

- Governor: `performance`, thermals flat (38°C), no throttling
- **Finding (FINDINGS.md §6):** NEON GDN kernels are **latency-bound** (serial dependency chain), not memory-bandwidth-bound at these problem sizes. Predicts O6 will be similar for fp32; quantization (int8/i8mm) is the path to bandwidth-boundness.
- Committed: `6759001`, `ff9eae2`

